{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJ9iNFtS5QJ8kZvHP2C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`saveAll` in `store.js` now waits for every write to finish before it resolves. The existing test passes, but I didn't add a test that reproduces the early-resolve case.\n\nThe cause was `items.forEach(async ...)`. `forEach` ignores the promises its callback returns, so the function returned `items.length` before any `db.put` had finished. A failed write also became an unhandled rejection, not a rejection of `saveAll`.\n\nI replaced it with `await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)))`. `saveAll` now resolves with the count only after all writes complete, and it rejects if any write fails, as the header comment says.\n\nThe writes still run concurrently, as they did before. If your db needs them in order or rate-limited, a sequential `for...of` loop with `await` would be the alternative."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":559,"cache_read_input_tokens":22804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":559},"output_tokens":268,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9331d14f-9a06-4d6f-b0d5-e26c66ad8448","uuid":"bea13fe8-b30b-4e87-99b6-f7a6d4e78df4","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:23:32.325Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJ9iGKXC5fA5mTZDGUg"}
